  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 77be8d3abc4d614408c62dfb3862c314, type: 3}
  m_Name: J1_Seq1_01
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::SpeakerTextSO
  showScore: 0
  dialogues:
  - character: {fileID: 11400000, guid: c8fcfa5882242b84b8bf1fb55659059e, type: 2}
    emotion: 1
    text: A client invites you to tender via a two stage for a new college in Sussex,
      for roughly 10-12 million pounds. There is a RIBA Stage 3 pack of drawings
      for the project. You and two other contractors accept the invite to tender.
  - character: {fileID: 11400000, guid: c8fcfa5882242b84b8bf1fb55659059e, type: 2}
    emotion: 0
    text: The client has worked with you before and was 80% happy with previous performance.
      You are starting with a score of 80% client satisfaction.
  - character: {fileID: 11400000, guid: c8fcfa5882242b84b8bf1fb55659059e, type: 2}
    emotion: 0
    text: Your standard overhead and profit is 10%. You are starting with a profit
      score of 10%.
